FULL GIDE FOR SETUP:


. WindowsOn Windows, Tkinter comes pre-installed with standard Python downloads. You only need to use the command prompt or terminal to install Pygame. [1] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y9VG3Pztok8), [2] (https://programming-24.mooc.fi/part-13/1-pygame/)Open Command Prompt or PowerShell and run:bashpip install pygame
Use code with caution.(If pip is not recognized, try running pip3 install pygame or python -m pip install pygame.) [1] (https://stackoverflow.com/questions/66070289/how-do-i-install-pygame-with-cmd), [2] (https://programming-24.mooc.fi/part-13/1-pygame/)2. macOSJust like Windows, Tkinter is generally included with official Python distributions on macOS.Open Terminal and run:bashpip3 install pygame
Use code with caution.3. Linux (Ubuntu / Debian / Mint)On Linux distributions, Python is split up. You have to install Tkinter using your system's package manager (apt), while Pygame is installed via pip. [1] (https://askubuntu.com/questions/399824/how-to-install-pygame), [2] (https://programming-24.mooc.fi/part-13/1-pygame/), [3] (http://stackoverflow.com/questions/4783810/install-tkinter-for-python)Open your Terminal and run:For Tkinter:bashsudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-tk
Use code with caution.For Pygame:bashpip3 install pygame --break-system-packages
Use code with caution.(Note: If your Linux distribution blocks global pip installations due to PEP 668, use a Python virtual environment or add the --break-system-packages flag if you want it globally). [1] (https://discuss.python.org/t/how-to-install-pygame-for-dummies/45778)How to Verify the InstallationsTo ensure both packages are installed correctly, launch a quick Python shell in your terminal:bashpython3
Use code with caution.(Or just python on Windows). [1] (https://programming-24.mooc.fi/part-13/1-pygame/), [2] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y9VG3Pztok8)
